{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-universally-injective}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dc7608cf91f05ba04a31b8acb23cf56e4948282f094c01a30ce36f56f5c6a8dc", "source_text": "Universally injective morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe2f0c6bcbcbe0a6167f53b713ef455cfaa7a3e8d8bbc9614d3914ff0f92a06e", "unit_id": "tag:0CI0:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfaee67d46ddd4d888702445be4244f6d5bf5b01389aeba0ea95707e8ecf77c4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:45de2c9cb5a6bcd352a26a67a9061485fcefcfe69a98a05d9dba94384dbff742", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks which is representable by\nalgebraic spaces. In\nProperties of Stacks, Section\n<REF_0001>\nwe have defined what it means for <MATH_0002> to be universally injective.\nHere is another characterization.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76365943d03a660a602c580147e6f63ad4ea4f4d8cf68b80d38a0535cc8e35b5", "unit_id": "tag:0CI0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Z}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-representable-universally-injective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d5aeb9363e6c0460c4d8ca174db9b6e52fab48bca0eb728566dbe3f6bc86cf4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8cbe477294bb05860c5b70e3a8615764996ce1fbd03db47c2d2b6408a1710ea9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of\nalgebraic stacks which is representable by algebraic spaces.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is universally injective (as in Properties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0001>), and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every morphism of algebraic stacks <MATH_0003>\nthe map <MATH_0004>\nis injective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4c90a235b4f9d49f5e84225489e7e6ea7ff171e7ac321ad72317e84a064ee77c", "unit_id": "tag:0CI1:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to V$", "MATH_0005": "$|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |V|$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[d] \\\\\n|V| \\ar[r] & |\\mathcal{Z}|\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\longrightarrow\n|V| \\times_{|\\mathcal{Z}|} |\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}|\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Rightarrow$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09aa1f8c8ad23cd19dc339d90766602caa1ad31ba2d799a54bf34d02f2619393", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7668aac8bcc5b963dac3b15bf2ea23887a19a6820f21ea6604ca67294517cde5", "source_text": "Assume (1), and let <MATH_0001> be as in (2).\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0003>.\nBy assumption the morphism <MATH_0004>\nof algebraic spaces is universally injective, in particular the map\n<MATH_0005> is injective. By\nProperties of Stacks, Section <REF_0001>\nin the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nthe horizontal arrows are open and surjective, and moreover\n<MATH_0007>\nis surjective. Hence as the left vertical arrow is injective it follows that\nthe right vertical arrow is injective. This proves (2).\nThe implication (2) <MATH_0008> (1) follows from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8e3db4a81cb733f569a3917b2454bc04b954d660d629e7b8c3c0962fcb754fa", "unit_id": "tag:0CI1:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CI0", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a26e1d54118693d3dcd58b8f43805892a0fda4b6a98036c9c1d349c5c89af604", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus we may use the following natural definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:35322e4680cc43900423677afa805c977a7e233dfb5b517fe59270b0a952b65f", "unit_id": "tag:0CI0:prose-0002"}
